  "methods": {
    "surfaces": "One cold 72000-face root mesh job. Dispatch/poll measures GUI submission/installation, excluding edge-cache building, material decoding, Bevy extraction and GPU work. Cooperative builder run on native for algorithm timings; browser timings are separate. Six-millisecond checks are soft and atomic work/scheduling can exceed the target.",
    "structure": "50001 shared empty instances. 3 warmups, 41 samples of one added/removed instance. Uncached baseline is the current cold validator, which already aggregates repeated children. Mutation is outside validation timing. Compare with incrementally invalidated graph counts, not whole editor commands.",
    "annotations": "5000 screen texts and 5000 detached dimensions across 100 definitions; 3 warmups and 41 SetUnits commands; all definitions remain shared, Undo/Redo asserted. Does not establish a numeric speedup for every linked-annotation workload. Linked vertices and cross-context invalidation have oracle correctness tests.",
    "memory": "Separate Linux process per fixture; /proc/self/status RSS/HWM plus GNU time maximum RSS. Load, save and 200 retained Undo steps followed by full Undo/Redo and document replacement. Native I/O retains compressed image payloads, not decoded GPU textures. RSS includes allocator-retained pages and cannot identify live allocations; slight /proc HWM variations are OS accounting artifacts. No conclusion of zero leaks or free history memory from flat RSS.",
    "environment": "Our compilations completed before native measurements; host activity and CPU frequency uncontrolled."
  },
